{
  "title": "Tour of the Tavern",
  "synopsis": "A guided sample project. Open each module in the left rail and read the encyclopedia article “Welcome — start here”. Synthetic content only.",
  "elements": [
    {
      "module_type": "encyclopedia",
      "title": "Welcome — start here",
      "metadata": {},
      "panels": [
        {
          "panel_type": "text",
          "title": "How to tour",
          "content": {
            "markdown": "Welcome to Tavern.\n\n1. Use **Modules / Items / Inspector / Tools** in the top bar to show or hide each menu (layout is remembered).\n2. On phones and tablets, those menus open as drawers over the canvas.\n3. Pick an item, then try **Focus** to clear the side menus while writing.\n4. Characters, Locations, Systems, Species, Cultures, Items, Arcs, Languages, and Religions use the panel canvas.\n5. Open **Relationships** to connect characters on the graph.\n6. **Maps** and **Timeline** show places and chronology.\n\nWhen you are done exploring, create your own project from the home page — this tour is safe to delete."
          }
        },
        {
          "panel_type": "attributes",
          "title": "Quick facts",
          "content": {
            "items": [
              { "key": "Purpose", "value": "Interactive tutorial" },
              { "key": "Safe to delete", "value": "Yes" }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module_type": "manuscript",
      "title": "Chapter 1 — First draft",
      "metadata": {},
      "body_markdown": "The lanterns along Saltglass Pier burned a soft green.\n\n[[Character:Mira Quill]] rolled her charts flat against the rail and whispered a tideworking cant. Far below, the water answered.\n\nUse **Save** after edits. Toggle **Source** for raw markdown. Set a **Goal** to track word count. Wiki links look like `[[Character:Name]]`.",
      "panels": []
    },
